# Benchmark path "village walk" (tools/ai/README.md "Benchmark states"). Starts where balcony_far.nxs ends (the balcony view, game step
# back to real time). The game step is fixed again (1/60 s per frame), so every run walks the same path in the same frames. The
# measurement window is the walk: from the log line "bench: village_walk start" to "bench: village_walk end" (~660 frames).
@rate 60
@log bench: village_walk start
# to the ladder and down it (forward on the stick climbs down here)
stick left 0 1 for 240
@shot walk_ladder
# let go near the bottom (B)
press B for 6
60
@shot walk_landed
# run sideways: the camera follows round the tree, past the houses into the open village (keeps away from the girl on the path,
# whose dialogue would stop the walk)
stick left -1 0 for 120
@shot walk_run1
stick left -1 0 for 120
@shot walk_run2
stick left -1 0 for 120
@shot walk_run3
@log bench: village_walk end
# still: compare these between runs (the path), the moving shots above are a frame or two apart between runs
60
@shot walk_end
@rate 0
@log bench: village_walk done
